    <!-- Shown in Settings › Accessibility for the keyboard-gesture
         pass-through service. -->
    <string name="passthrough_service_label">WM Keyboard gestures</string>
    <string name="passthrough_service_summary">Keeps WM Keyboard\'s gestures working with a screen reader</string>
    <string name="passthrough_service_description">This service keeps the keyboard gestures available while a screen reader runs. The gestures are the spacebar cursor slide, the backspace word swipe, glide typing and handwriting.\n\nThe service reads nothing. It receives no accessibility events. It cannot see the screen content. Its only action is to mark the keyboard window to pass touches straight through. Every touch outside the keyboard still goes to your screen reader as usual.</string>
    <string name="split_screen_helper_service_label">WM Keyboard split screen</string>
    <string name="split_screen_helper_service_summary">Lets the app launcher open apps in split screen on phones where it otherwise opens them full screen</string>
    <string name="split_screen_helper_service_description">When you open an app in split screen from WM Keyboard\'s app launcher, or open a split screen pair, this service presses Android\'s split screen switch, the same one the Recents menu has. Then the app opens in the free half.\n\nBefore pressing it, the service checks whether split screen is already up, from where the app windows are on screen. It never reads what is in them. It does nothing at any other time, does not watch what you type and keeps nothing.</string>
    <string name="screen_context_service_label">WM Keyboard AI screen reading</string>
    <string name="screen_context_service_summary">Lets the floating button\'s Ask AI and Look up read the text on screen when you use them</string>
    <string name="screen_context_service_description">When you press Ask AI on WM Keyboard\'s floating button, this service reads the text of the app on screen once and puts it in a new AI chat, where you see it before anything is sent. When you use Look up on the floating button and tap a word, it reads the text under your finger once and looks that word up in your dictionaries.\n\nIt reads nothing at any other time. It does not perform actions, does not watch what you type and keeps no copy. Text in password fields is skipped. Where the chat is sent depends on the AI provider you chose in WM Keyboard\'s settings, or it stays on the phone with an on-device model.</string>
